      "note": "The README identifies the jam, initial development duration, and theme. “The House Always Wins is a game originally created within 48 hours for the\n[GMTK Game Jam 2022](https://itch.io/jam/gmtk-jam-2022).” (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/krobbi/gmtk-2022/main/readme.md)\nThe project identifies the game but contains no config/features version declaration. “config/name=\"The House Always Wins\"” (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/krobbi/gmtk-2022/main/project.godot)\nSelecting altered odds consumes mana in proportion to the change. “var cost: int = int(abs(new_odds - odds) / 2.0)\n\todds = new_odds\n\tmana -= cost” (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/krobbi/gmtk-2022/main/entities/game_manager/game_manager.gd)\nThe dice implementation uses a 2D body despite its perspective-style presentation. “extends KinematicBody2D” (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/krobbi/gmtk-2022/main/entities/die/die.gd)\nThe release provides a Windows download alongside macOS and Linux archives. “the-house-always-wins-windows.zip” (https://ruxaroh.itch.io/the-house-always-wins)\nThe author describes the central odds-rigging casino premise. “As a fey with the power to manipulate odds and read minds you have been captured and tasked with running and rigging a game of dice at a local casino.” (https://ruxaroh.itch.io/the-house-always-wins)\nThe stated Creative Commons license applies to background music, not the code. “Creative Commons CC BY-SA 3.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0” (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/krobbi/gmtk-2022/main/readme.md)"
